<!-- @opening -->
<p class="story-lead">Requests keep failing after the dependency stops responding. During the cool-down, calls are rejected quickly. When a probe is allowed, its outcome determines whether normal calls can return.</p>

<!-- @before 5. Failure Modes & Tradeoffs :: staff -->
### Check which result can change the breaker

Trace a slow call that began before the breaker opened and completes after a probe starts. The example tracks a generation and permit so an old result cannot close the newer breaker state. Check both the probe limit and the outcome of a failed probe. [Resilience4j circuit breaker states](https://resilience4j.readme.io/docs/circuitbreaker).
